# Sprinting extras (SPEC Sprinting: Camera, Sneaking). FOV is data/input.toml's
# fov_degrees (70) widening by fov_extra_degrees (10) over fov_ease_seconds (0.15).
# The water rule (no sprint start in water, entering water ends it) is covered
# by the "running off the islet" case in sprint.input and the Rust tests (#862).

case the FOV widens during a sprint and eases back after it
start walk raft
click
lock
runway 12
frame 50 x2
expect fov ~ 70
press KeyW
frame 50 x2
down KeyW
frame 50 x2
expect sprinting = true
expect fov > 70
frame 50 x6
expect fov ~ 80
up KeyW
frame 50 x6
expect sprinting = false
expect fov ~ 70

case starting to sneak during a sprint ends it and the FOV eases back
start walk raft
click
lock
runway 12
press KeyW
frame 50 x2
down KeyW
frame 50 x6
expect sprinting = true
expect fov ~ 80
down ShiftLeft
frame 50 x6
expect sprinting = false
expect fov ~ 70

case a double-tap while sneaking does not start a sprint
start walk raft
click
lock
runway 12
down ShiftLeft
press KeyW
frame 50 x2
down KeyW
frame 50 x6
expect sprinting = false
expect fov ~ 70

# Head-on wall rule (docs/design/sprinting.md Phase B, #1331, #1334): a shallow
# angle against the wall slides along it and keeps the sprint.
case sliding along a wall at a shallow angle keeps the sprint
start walk raft
click
lock
runway 1
mouse 560 0
press KeyW
frame 50 x2
down KeyW
frame 50 x2
expect sprinting = true
frame 50 x6
expect sprinting = true
expect moved.z > -1

case a sprint-jump keeps the sprint going
start walk raft
click
lock
runway 12
press KeyW
frame 50 x2
down KeyW
frame 50 x6
expect sprinting = true
press Space
frame 50 x2
expect sprinting = true
